@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="pt-BR">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="utf-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+  <title></title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/curso.css">
+</head>
+<body>
+  <curso-pagina>
+    <h1>Referências</h1>
+
+    <div class="referencias">
+      <section class="referencias__modulo">
+        <h2 class="estilo-h1">Módulo 1: Introdução, Histórico da IA e Grandes Modelos de Linguagem</h2>
+        <p>ABRÀMOFF, M. D. <i>et al.</i> Pivotal trial of an autonomous AI-based diagnostic system for detection of diabetic retinopathy in primary care offices. <strong>npj Digital Medicine</strong>, v. 1, art. 39, 2018. DOI: 10.1038/s41746-018-0040-6.</p>
+        <p>CHIANG, W.-L. <i>et al.</i> Chatbot Arena: an open platform for evaluating LLMs by human preference. <i>In</i>: INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON MACHINE LEARNING, 41., 2024, Viena. <strong>Proceedings</strong> [...]. Viena: ICML, 2024. DOI: 10.48550/arXiv.2403.04132.</p>
+        <p>HAENLEIN, M.; KAPLAN, A. A brief history of artificial intelligence: on the past, present, and future of artificial intelligence. <strong>California Management Review</strong>, v. 61, n. 4, p. 5–14, 2019. DOI: 10.1177/0008125619864925.</p>
+        <p>HOFSTADTER, D. R. <strong>Gödel, Escher, Bach</strong>: um entrelaçamento de gênios brilhantes. Tradução: José Viegas Filho. Brasília, DF: Editora da UnB; São Paulo: Imprensa Oficial do Estado, 2001.</p>
+        <p>JUMPER, J. <i>et al.</i> Highly accurate protein structure prediction with AlphaFold. <strong>Nature</strong>, v. 596, n. 7873, p. 583-589, ago. 2021. DOI: 10.1038/s41586-021-03819-2.</p>
+        <p>McCORDUCK, P. <strong>Machines who think</strong>: a personal inquiry into the history and prospects of artificial intelligence. 2. ed. Natick: A. K. Peters, 2004.</p>
